      "worked": "Let $AC=b\\,\\mathrm{cm}$. By the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}25&=b^2+4^2-2(b)(4)\\cos120^\\circ\\\\25&=b^2+16+4b\\\\b^2+4b-9&=0\\\\(b+2)^2&=13\\\\b&=\\sqrt{13}-2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe positive root is required because $b$ is a length. Using the area rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(4)(\\sqrt{13}-2)\\sin120^\\circ\\\\A&=\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{13}-2)\\\\A&=(\\sqrt{39}-2\\sqrt{3})\\,\\mathrm{cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
